00:46:13.228 --> 00:46:15.731
[Joe] I figured he was using
the same aliases.

723
00:46:15.814 --> 00:46:18.484
I figured he'd go to the places
he'd been before.

724
00:46:18.567 --> 00:46:20.778
Phoenix, Florida, Georgia,
and... and Kentucky.

725
00:46:20.861 --> 00:46:21.862
[phone ringing]

726
00:46:21.945 --> 00:46:24.990
So I put a stop on all of his aliases.

727
00:46:25.949 --> 00:46:27.910
[Billy] They alerted
all the different states

728
00:46:27.993 --> 00:46:32.623
where he had obtained
a driver's license under different names,

729
00:46:32.706 --> 00:46:35.417
thinking that he might
try to renew a driver's license.

730
00:46:35.501 --> 00:46:37.419
[pensive music playing]

731
00:46:39.505 --> 00:46:40.756
[Joe] Sure enough,

732
00:46:41.381 --> 00:46:44.468
he renewed that driver's license
under Warren Marshall

733
00:46:44.551 --> 00:46:46.261
in Louisville, Kentucky.

734
00:46:50.641 --> 00:46:52.100
And I flew to Kentucky,

735
00:46:52.935 --> 00:46:57.397
and we had an agent in Louisville
dress up in a UPS uniform.

736
00:46:57.481 --> 00:46:58.899
[suspenseful music playing]

737
00:46:59.733 --> 00:47:03.695
Arrest procedure had to be
delivering his driver's license to him

738
00:47:03.779 --> 00:47:05.656
and arresting him at that time.

739
00:47:05.739 --> 00:47:07.741
[music continues]

740
00:47:13.330 --> 00:47:15.123
[music intensifies]

741
00:47:15.207 --> 00:47:16.333
[siren wailing]

742
00:47:16.416 --> 00:47:18.544
And we delivered the driver's license.

743
00:47:23.924 --> 00:47:25.467
And agents surrounded him

744
00:47:26.218 --> 00:47:27.970
and took him into custody.

745
00:47:41.859 --> 00:47:45.737
Immediately following his arrest,
agents went to his residence,

746
00:47:45.821 --> 00:47:47.281
talked to all the neighbors.

747
00:47:47.364 --> 00:47:49.783
[reporter] Floyd lived
in this rundown apartment building,

748
00:47:49.867 --> 00:47:52.703
just east of downtown Louisville,
about six weeks.

749
00:47:52.786 --> 00:47:56.039
Not long enough for his neighbors
to know much about him.

750
00:47:56.123 --> 00:47:58.500
To my knowledge,
he didn't even talk to anybody.

751
00:47:58.584 --> 00:48:00.043
Just came in and came out.

752
00:48:00.127 --> 00:48:04.131
Didn't talk to anybody
about family or anything like that, so...

753
00:48:04.214 --> 00:48:06.216
No one had seen Michael.

754
00:48:07.175 --> 00:48:11.388
I checked with both employments
where he was presently employed

755
00:48:11.471 --> 00:48:13.223
and with his previous employ as a painter.

756
00:48:14.391 --> 00:48:15.809
No one had seen Michael.

757
00:48:17.936 --> 00:48:19.646
He had a bus ticket

758
00:48:19.730 --> 00:48:23.442
from Atlanta, Georgia
to Louisville, Kentucky

759
00:48:23.525 --> 00:48:25.819
for one person and one person only.

760
00:48:34.036 --> 00:48:36.246
He's my son, I love him very much.

761
00:48:36.330 --> 00:48:38.040
[keys jingling]

762
00:48:38.123 --> 00:48:39.666
I hope that they find him.

763
00:48:40.500 --> 00:48:45.172
[Joe] The next day, I sat him down and...
and I asked if Michael was still alive.

764
00:48:47.507 --> 00:48:49.509
And he claimed that he was.

765
00:48:49.593 --> 00:48:52.095
He said he left him with a rich person.

766
00:48:52.179 --> 00:48:55.307
There's no rich person who
has anything to do with Franklin Floyd.

767
00:48:56.892 --> 00:49:00.854
They were all such ridiculous statements.
This... This is another one of his lies.

768
00:49:00.938 --> 00:49:02.940
[solemn music playing]

769
00:49:08.195 --> 00:49:11.615
At this point,
I felt certain Michael was dead.

770
00:49:11.698 --> 00:49:15.786
But it... it's a child,
and you... you hope you're wrong.

771
00:49:16.954 --> 00:49:18.080
[cameras clicking]

772
00:49:19.206 --> 00:49:20.207
We miss Michael.

773
00:49:21.875 --> 00:49:23.293
He's like a son to us.

774
00:49:27.172 --> 00:49:28.340
Michael, we love you.

775
00:49:29.091 --> 00:49:32.344
Uh, if we knew where to come to get you,
we'd come get you

776
00:49:32.427 --> 00:49:33.679
but we don't know where.

777
00:49:36.223 --> 00:49:40.978
There'd be many times that we'd be driving
down the road and I'd see a kid in a car

778
00:49:41.061 --> 00:49:43.271
and the hair was
the same color as Michael's,

779
00:49:43.355 --> 00:49:45.774
and I'd try to get up beside him
and see it wasn't Michael.

780
00:49:45.857 --> 00:49:47.359
But there's... there's always,

781
00:49:48.151 --> 00:49:50.320
you know,
until you get the final definite,

782
00:49:50.404 --> 00:49:53.490
there's always that thought
that maybe he's still out there.

783
00:49:54.658 --> 00:49:56.201
There's just something about him.

784
00:49:56.284 --> 00:50:01.248
The way he looks, his big brown eyes
that conveys the love that he has for us.

785
00:50:01.331 --> 00:50:05.127
We have that same love for him
and we just want to have him back.

786
00:50:05.669 --> 00:50:07.004
[sniffling]

787
00:50:07.087 --> 00:50:08.588
[cameras clicking]

788
00:50:08.672 --> 00:50:10.674
[siren wailing in distance]

789
00:50:12.009 --> 00:50:14.011
[birds chirping]

790
00:50:16.013 --> 00:50:17.973
[Joe] As this case was set up for trial,

791
00:50:18.056 --> 00:50:22.728
we realized that charging Floyd
for Michael's murder on its merits is weak

792
00:50:22.811 --> 00:50:24.479
because we don't have a body.

793
00:50:24.980 --> 00:50:26.690
It would be a hard case to win.

794
00:50:32.654 --> 00:50:35.532
[man] You can make a murder case
without a body.

795
00:50:35.615 --> 00:50:37.535
But we know that
if we're gonna get a conviction,

796
00:50:37.617 --> 00:50:39.828
we have to prove it
beyond a reasonable doubt.

797
00:50:39.911 --> 00:50:41.163
And at this point,

798
00:50:42.414 --> 00:50:43.498
it's a close call.

799
00:50:43.582 --> 00:50:48.253
So what seemed like a pretty
straightforward and easy case to prove

800
00:50:48.336 --> 00:50:52.424
was really not that easy a case.
We had some hurdles we had overcome.

801
00:50:53.050 --> 00:50:56.428
So we charged him with
kidnapping Michael Hughes,

802
00:50:56.511 --> 00:50:59.639
carjacking,
using a firearm during the carjacking,

803
00:50:59.723 --> 00:51:03.351
which added a five-year minimum
mandatory sentence on to that.

804
00:51:03.435 --> 00:51:06.772
We also charged him
with a second firearm offense

805
00:51:06.855 --> 00:51:10.275
for using the firearm
during the commission of the kidnapping.

806
00:51:10.901 --> 00:51:13.236
That added an additional 25-year sentence.

807
00:51:16.198 --> 00:51:19.868
[Billy] The first time I saw him was when
he was being escorted into federal court.

808
00:51:19.951 --> 00:51:23.747
He just had this empty, deadly stare.

809
00:51:24.581 --> 00:51:27.834
That stare was a Charlie Manson stare.

810
00:51:28.335 --> 00:51:29.836
It was scary to me.

811
00:51:30.587 --> 00:51:32.255
[tense music playing]

812
00:51:32.339 --> 00:51:35.008
[reporter] Is justice going to be
served here, Mr. Floyd?

813
00:51:40.555 --> 00:51:45.310
Floyd started off defending himself
and... and he was very aggressive,

814
00:51:45.393 --> 00:51:46.770
asking dumb questions.

815
00:51:49.106 --> 00:51:52.109
He knew that this judge may allow him

816
00:51:52.192 --> 00:51:56.404
to argue his case, and have
what we call hybrid representation.

817
00:51:56.488 --> 00:51:59.407
He wanted to get up and tell the story.
He wanted to talk.

818
00:51:59.950 --> 00:52:02.577
And the only way he could do that
without taking the witness stand

819
00:52:02.661 --> 00:52:04.746
was to be able to argue to the judge.

820
00:52:07.666 --> 00:52:10.001
He would ramble and go off on tangents.

821
00:52:10.085 --> 00:52:14.673
It was just ego, hubris,
narcissistic personality,

822
00:52:14.756 --> 00:52:16.716
sociopathic personality.

823
00:52:20.637 --> 00:52:23.348
[Jenny] I testified
in Michael's kidnapping trial.

824
00:52:23.431 --> 00:52:27.352
The hardest thing, terrifying,
was having to face him in court.

825
00:52:28.937 --> 00:52:31.189
To testify with him sitting right there.

826
00:52:32.732 --> 00:52:34.776
And I remember on the stand,

827
00:52:34.860 --> 00:52:38.280
looking over
and staring right in his eyes.

828
00:52:39.156 --> 00:52:43.577
And, like, "I got you. I got you, fucker."

829
00:52:43.660 --> 00:52:45.662
[music continues]

830
00:52:46.872 --> 00:52:50.041
[Billy] Floyd got up
to ask her a question.

831
00:52:50.584 --> 00:52:54.546
You drew your opinion
about me in the way I am

832
00:52:54.629 --> 00:52:57.799
based on the information
that the FBI told you, right?

833
00:52:58.758 --> 00:53:04.806
And she said, "No, I drew my opinion
about you when I saw the type of lingerie

834
00:53:04.890 --> 00:53:07.976
you were buying your daughter
and how you made her dress.

835
00:53:08.059 --> 00:53:10.729
That's when I drew my opinion about you.

836
00:53:11.479 --> 00:53:15.817
And I looked right in the face and I said,
"You are her daddy."

837
00:53:15.901 --> 00:53:18.737
"She called you daddy.
You were her father."

838
00:53:19.404 --> 00:53:23.366
And his... his attorney
just threw his papers up in the air.

839
00:53:23.450 --> 00:53:25.118
There was nothing they could do.

840
00:53:26.453 --> 00:53:28.330
[Mark] Look, it was not an easy case.

841
00:53:28.413 --> 00:53:30.624
It... It was all circumstantial.

842
00:53:30.707 --> 00:53:33.001
I mean, that's what gave me heartburn.

843
00:53:37.339 --> 00:53:39.925
I've never lost a case at trial. Never.

844
00:53:40.967 --> 00:53:45.347
But every time, at the end of trial,
you get butterflies in your stomach.

845
00:53:48.058 --> 00:53:51.728
The judge released the order
and we were successful on all counts.

846
00:53:56.233 --> 00:54:00.737
After evading the law for two decades,
he was sentenced to 52 years in prison,

847
00:54:00.820 --> 00:54:03.365
no parole,
for the kidnapping of Michael Hughes.

848
00:54:06.326 --> 00:54:08.703
[reporters clamoring]

849
00:54:08.787 --> 00:54:12.067
- [reporter] Mr. Floyd, what do you think?
- Fuck you and Oklahoma, son of a bitch.

850
00:54:12.123 --> 00:54:14.477
- Fuck off, you motherfucker!
- [reporter 2] Where's the boy?

851
00:54:14.501 --> 00:54:15.627
Fuck you!

852
00:54:19.381 --> 00:54:21.925
[ominous music plays]

853
00:54:22.008 --> 00:54:23.635
[Joe] Then I got a call from an agent.

854
00:54:23.718 --> 00:54:27.430
They found the principal's truck,
which Floyd stole in the kidnapping.

855
00:54:29.140 --> 00:54:32.560
And they found photographs
that'd been taped underneath the truck.

856
00:54:32.644 --> 00:54:34.020
[suspenseful music plays]

857
00:54:35.313 --> 00:54:37.774
They were all, almost all

858
00:54:39.734 --> 00:54:40.734
obscene.

859
00:54:41.069 --> 00:54:42.069
Pornography.

860
00:54:44.447 --> 00:54:49.035
It was very obviously Floyd's
because included in these photographs

861
00:54:49.119 --> 00:54:51.913
were some photographs of Sharon
when she was small.

862
00:54:56.626 --> 00:55:00.630
Also, in these photographs,
was a young lady we hadn't seen before.

863
00:55:02.340 --> 00:55:05.552
She was in various stages
of being disrobed and beaten.

864
00:55:09.139 --> 00:55:15.061
And I said, "He could not have beaten her
to this extent and not killed her."

865
00:55:15.145 --> 00:55:16.146
He'd had to.

866
00:55:18.273 --> 00:55:19.733
We had another mystery.

867
00:55:19.816 --> 00:55:20.816
Who was she?

868
00:55:22.277 --> 00:55:25.989
Looking at her, she had...
she had real tan lines.

869
00:55:26.698 --> 00:55:30.660
And I go, "Well, they could've spent time
in Florida, Georgia, and Kentucky."

870
00:55:31.244 --> 00:55:33.997
So I sent the photographs
down to those offices

871
00:55:34.080 --> 00:55:36.541
and asked them to check
their unsolved cases.

872
00:55:36.624 --> 00:55:39.127
Now this is what you call
a shot in the dark.

873
00:55:42.130 --> 00:55:44.716
[newsreader] <i>A highway crew
makes a grisly discovery.</i>

874
00:55:44.799 --> 00:55:47.344
<i>A badly decomposed human skull.</i>

875
00:55:47.427 --> 00:55:50.847
<i>Four days of digging
produces 90 percent of a skeleton,</i>

876
00:55:50.930 --> 00:55:54.142
<i>along with a breast implant,
and some clothing and jewelry.</i>

877
00:55:57.896 --> 00:56:01.858
When we examined the skull, we found
two bullet holes to the back of the skull

878
00:56:01.941 --> 00:56:04.944
and the orbital bone was broken
under one of the eyes.

879
00:56:05.028 --> 00:56:07.655
It was definitely not a natural death.

880
00:56:07.739 --> 00:56:10.367
There was definitely
homicidal violence involved in it.

881
00:56:10.450 --> 00:56:12.869
So, yes, it was classified as a homicide
almost immediately.

882
00:56:14.329 --> 00:56:17.624
We looked at all of the local agencies.

883
00:56:17.707 --> 00:56:20.627
We weren't able to identify the skeleton.

884
00:56:21.753 --> 00:56:24.631
About a year later,
we got notified by the FBI

885
00:56:25.256 --> 00:56:29.677
that they had photos from another case
of a young lady that was being beaten.

886
00:56:30.929 --> 00:56:32.180
And as we look at them,

887
00:56:32.263 --> 00:56:34.743
the shirt wrapped around
the neck of the girl who's been beaten

888
00:56:34.808 --> 00:56:37.435
matches the shirt
that we have tied in a knot.

889
00:56:37.519 --> 00:56:42.065
We went ahead and got dental records
from them and Jane Doe I-275,

890
00:56:42.148 --> 00:56:43.775
which is what she was known as.

891
00:56:45.068 --> 00:56:47.153
And we were able to actually identify

892
00:56:47.821 --> 00:56:50.073
the skeleton
on the side of the interstate.

893
00:56:50.156 --> 00:56:51.408
Ms. Cheryl Commesso.

894
00:56:54.577 --> 00:56:57.831
And during our investigation,
we discovered that Cheryl had worked

895
00:56:57.914 --> 00:57:00.750
as an exotic dancer at the Mons Venus.

896
00:57:03.878 --> 00:57:05.755
[newsreader]
<i>Now, police want to talk to anyone</i>

897
00:57:05.839 --> 00:57:08.883
<i>who knew Cheryl Commesso back in 1989.</i>

898
00:57:22.188 --> 00:57:25.275
[Heather] After the videotape
of Cheryl and Sharon,

899
00:57:30.864 --> 00:57:33.867
there just was a lot of gossip going on.

900
00:57:33.950 --> 00:57:36.369
Everyone in the club was talking about it.

901
00:57:39.330 --> 00:57:42.333
And then Cheryl showed up at the club.

902
00:57:44.002 --> 00:57:48.339
And she had a bruise on her cheek,
a black eye.

903
00:57:48.423 --> 00:57:50.717
She had marks on her neck

904
00:57:50.800 --> 00:57:53.136
where you could see
she had been strangled.

905
00:57:55.930 --> 00:58:01.060
And that's when I knew that this had gone
from Warren being a twisted pervert

906
00:58:01.144 --> 00:58:03.313
to him being physical.

907
00:58:05.523 --> 00:58:07.901
And he was obsessed with her.

908
00:58:07.984 --> 00:58:09.903
He called many times to the club

909
00:58:10.528 --> 00:58:13.948
and he was asking me
a lot of questions about Cheryl.

910
00:58:14.032 --> 00:58:16.075
He wanted to know her last name.

911
00:58:16.159 --> 00:58:18.328
He wanted to know where her dad lived.

912
00:58:20.622 --> 00:58:23.416
Every time he called and asked for Cheryl,

913
00:58:23.500 --> 00:58:26.878
I would tell him that
she isn't here and then I'd hang up.

914
00:58:28.546 --> 00:58:29.964
We did everything we could

915
00:58:30.048 --> 00:58:32.926
to try to create separation
between the two of them.

916
00:58:36.471 --> 00:58:40.308
But shortly after that,
I was walking out of the club.

917
00:58:41.726 --> 00:58:43.853
Sharon's dad was in the parking lot.

918
00:58:43.937 --> 00:58:45.939
[suspenseful music playing]

919
00:58:48.316 --> 00:58:52.278
And Cheryl was standing next to his car
and they're having a heated argument.

920
00:58:54.239 --> 00:58:55.782
And he was screaming at her.

921
00:58:57.200 --> 00:58:59.536
And he said he was going to kill her.

922
00:59:02.121 --> 00:59:05.375
So, I ran over there. I intervened.

923
00:59:07.293 --> 00:59:10.755
Then he got mad at me,
and he revved his car at me

924
00:59:10.838 --> 00:59:12.465
and the car lurched.

925
00:59:12.549 --> 00:59:15.468
He was acting like
he was going to hit me with the car.

926
00:59:18.638 --> 00:59:20.390
I walked away holding her,

927
00:59:21.015 --> 00:59:22.684
walked her to her car.

928
00:59:22.767 --> 00:59:25.186
I thought she would go home to her dad.

929
00:59:25.770 --> 00:59:28.273
And that was the last time I saw Cheryl.

930
00:59:31.568 --> 00:59:33.278
[music fades]

931
00:59:35.321 --> 00:59:38.324
[Michelle] All of a sudden,
Sharon and Warren had to go out of town.

932
00:59:38.408 --> 00:59:41.452
And they asked if I could collect the mail
and keep my eyes on the trailer.

933
00:59:42.996 --> 00:59:45.957
And one night,
the neighbor right across the street

934
00:59:46.040 --> 00:59:48.543
went outside
to smoke a cigarette out on the porch,

935
00:59:48.626 --> 00:59:50.211
and there was a guy in a truck.

936
00:59:52.380 --> 00:59:56.009
And he gets out of the truck,
goes around to Sharon and Warren's house.

937
00:59:57.760 --> 01:00:01.180
About five minutes later, he comes out,
gets in the truck, takes off.

938
01:00:01.764 --> 01:00:04.183
Flicks his cigarette, comes inside,
and he said...

939
01:00:04.267 --> 01:00:06.394
"All of a sudden I hear this boom!"

940
01:00:07.520 --> 01:00:09.772
He looked out the window
and there's this big ol'...

941
01:00:09.856 --> 01:00:11.733
[exploding]

942
01:00:11.816 --> 01:00:15.486
Right through the center. And like,
literally, the stove went through the...

943
01:00:15.570 --> 01:00:17.155
Like just... [mimics blast]

944
01:00:18.197 --> 01:00:20.658
People, you know,
that were chitter-chatting,

945
01:00:20.742 --> 01:00:23.411
you know, by the pool, by the mailbox,
you know, that...

946
01:00:24.829 --> 01:00:29.584
Warren had hired somebody
or made somebody, uh,

947
01:00:30.418 --> 01:00:31.794
burn down his trailer.

948
01:00:36.591 --> 01:00:39.719
[Joe] We finally knew
why Floyd left Florida in such a hurry.

949
01:00:41.596 --> 01:00:44.557
He was fleeing because
he had killed Cheryl Commesso.

950
01:00:48.895 --> 01:00:52.190
Floyd knew that law enforcement
would be looking for

951
01:00:52.273 --> 01:00:55.526
a man, his daughter, and her child.

952
01:00:55.610 --> 01:00:59.614
They would not be looking for a man,
his wife, and their child.

953
01:01:00.531 --> 01:01:02.784
And that's why they stopped
and got married.

954
01:01:03.451 --> 01:01:05.453
[pensive music playing]

955
01:01:15.713 --> 01:01:18.716
[newsreader] <i>The story of Floyd's
criminal life spans half the nation,</i>

956
01:01:18.800 --> 01:01:21.135
<i>from Oklahoma,
where his wife turned up dead,</i>

957
01:01:21.219 --> 01:01:24.430
<i>he kidnapped his son
and abducted a school principal,</i>

958
01:01:24.514 --> 01:01:27.392
<i>to this underbrush, near Interstate 275,</i>

959
01:01:27.475 --> 01:01:30.228
<i>where the skeletal remains
of Cheryl Commesso turned up.</i>

960
01:01:30.311 --> 01:01:32.146
<i>Former detective Mark Deasaro says</i>

961
01:01:32.230 --> 01:01:34.941
<i>Floyd will murder again
if he ever gets out of prison.</i>

962
01:01:35.024 --> 01:01:37.402
<i>He's a... He's a sociopath and a predator.</i>

963
01:01:37.485 --> 01:01:39.965
Floyd was charged with first-degree murder
for Cheryl Commesso.

964
01:01:40.029 --> 01:01:42.073
[ominous music plays]

965
01:01:45.284 --> 01:01:47.078
[Mark] I always felt
that we had a good case

966
01:01:47.161 --> 01:01:48.601
when you looked at all the evidence,

967
01:01:48.663 --> 01:01:51.082
even though, the majority of it
may have been circumstantial.

968
01:01:51.165 --> 01:01:54.043
It was just overwhelming,
the fact that we could put her there,

969
01:01:54.127 --> 01:01:56.337
we could put him there.
We could put them together.

970
01:01:56.421 --> 01:01:58.923
We had people that observed arguments
between them.

971
01:01:59.006 --> 01:02:03.094
Franklin Floyd faces lethal injection
for the murder of a Tampa nude dancer.

972
01:02:03.177 --> 01:02:04.804
[ominous music plays]

973
01:02:06.889 --> 01:02:09.684
[Michelle] The detectives, they asked me
to identify some photos.

974
01:02:10.935 --> 01:02:14.897
There's a photo
of Cheryl's body laying on that mattress.

975
01:02:14.981 --> 01:02:18.317
The exact same dirty, nasty mattress

976
01:02:19.026 --> 01:02:21.654
on that hide-a-bed in his living room.

977
01:02:24.574 --> 01:02:29.203
I was in that man's house
at least seven times a week.

978
01:02:31.372 --> 01:02:33.499
And out of those seven times,

979
01:02:33.583 --> 01:02:36.127
every day that couch was open.

980
01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:40.548
There was no... no misrepresentation.

981
01:02:40.631 --> 01:02:43.259
That was the same mattress.

982
01:02:44.135 --> 01:02:46.179
I knew. I was...

983
01:02:47.930 --> 01:02:48.930
Yeah.

984
01:02:49.265 --> 01:02:51.350
We had Floyd for 52 years.

985
01:02:52.059 --> 01:02:56.773
But now we had a chance to convict
Floyd on a murder investigation.

986
01:02:56.856 --> 01:03:00.151
A capital crime,
for which he could get the death sentence.

987
01:03:06.783 --> 01:03:09.076
Franklin was found guilty
of first-degree murder.

988
01:03:11.412 --> 01:03:12.914
He was sentenced to death.

989
01:03:15.708 --> 01:03:18.169
[Joe] It was a very good feeling
to hear the verdict.

990
01:03:18.252 --> 01:03:21.839
There was a great deal of satisfaction
in knowing that Floyd was going to be

991
01:03:21.923 --> 01:03:24.133
where he couldn't hurt anybody.

992
01:03:29.222 --> 01:03:33.476
Now, the bad aspect of this case,
even after trial is

993
01:03:35.186 --> 01:03:36.771
I had no idea where Michael...

994
01:03:37.355 --> 01:03:38.439
the body is.

995
01:03:44.946 --> 01:03:48.908
[Billy] It was just a freak accident
that those photos were found,

996
01:03:48.991 --> 01:03:52.954
and he eventually got convicted
of a homicide.

997
01:03:53.037 --> 01:03:55.456
Uh, it wasn't the one we wished to have.

998
01:03:56.040 --> 01:04:01.796
But I think in every police officer's
career there's something that lingers.

999
01:04:05.299 --> 01:04:07.885
I took a picture of Michael Anthony Hughes

1000
01:04:07.969 --> 01:04:10.847
and I actually taped that
right above my computer,

1001
01:04:10.930 --> 01:04:12.974
where I had to look at it every day.

1002
01:04:13.057 --> 01:04:15.810
It was something that just gave me hope.
That's what it did.

1003
01:04:15.893 --> 01:04:18.980
It kept me going
every day at the office, like...

1004
01:04:20.147 --> 01:04:23.025
We need to not come to this.
And it will happen.

1005
01:04:23.109 --> 01:04:24.235
Someday.

1006
01:04:25.653 --> 01:04:27.947
When I left, it was still taped there.

1007
01:04:28.030 --> 01:04:32.702
And as I clean my office to leave,
I finally took that picture off.

1008
01:04:33.411 --> 01:04:35.997
And retired.

1009
01:04:42.587 --> 01:04:45.256
In the 27 years I worked for the FBI,

1010
01:04:45.339 --> 01:04:47.592
I've come awfully close
to closing every case.

1011
01:04:52.763 --> 01:04:56.601
Two of them that I was not able to close
at the time I retired

1012
01:04:57.101 --> 01:05:00.563
was finding Michael
and identifying Sharon.

1013
01:05:00.646 --> 01:05:02.648
[solemn music playing]

1014
01:05:30.259 --> 01:05:33.679
[man] In 2002, a friend
just sent me a photograph,

1015
01:05:33.763 --> 01:05:35.598
saying you have to look at this.

1016
01:05:35.681 --> 01:05:38.601
It was a picture
on what was called the Doe Network.

1017
01:05:38.684 --> 01:05:40.394
It was a missing person website.

1018
01:05:41.479 --> 01:05:43.481
And it was a picture of a little girl

1019
01:05:44.231 --> 01:05:47.860
sitting in the lap of a man
that was supposed to be her father.

1020
01:05:47.944 --> 01:05:54.450
And the caption was underneath
that she had been kidnapped,

1021
01:05:55.534 --> 01:06:01.040
raised as his daughter
and married and killed.

1022
01:06:01.791 --> 01:06:03.167
And I said, "Oh my God."

1023
01:06:03.250 --> 01:06:06.921
But then more you looked at the picture,
and the more you looked at her,

1024
01:06:07.004 --> 01:06:09.298
you could see
something was terribly wrong.

1025
01:06:11.050 --> 01:06:13.761
And I just looked at it and said,
"I have to dig into this."

1026
01:06:13.844 --> 01:06:17.682
The first person I think
I spoke with was Joe Fitzpatrick.

1027
01:06:17.765 --> 01:06:19.767
[suspenseful music playing

1028
01:06:21.018 --> 01:06:25.356
And he says that there were two mysteries
that he had hoped to resolve.

1029
01:06:26.524 --> 01:06:28.067
Who is Sharon Marshall,

1030
01:06:28.150 --> 01:06:30.277
and what happened to Michael Hughes?

1031
01:06:30.361 --> 01:06:32.238
[indistinct chatter]

1032
01:06:32.321 --> 01:06:34.782
And even though
he was kind of leery talk to me,

1033
01:06:34.865 --> 01:06:37.827
you could tell that
there was some unfinished business here.

1034
01:06:39.704 --> 01:06:41.789
This case meant something to Joe.

1035
01:06:41.872 --> 01:06:46.919
And he was really affected
by the girl that was in the picture.

1036
01:06:49.380 --> 01:06:50.381
It was her.

1037
01:06:51.340 --> 01:06:52.340
It was Sharon.

1038
01:06:52.842 --> 01:06:53.842
It was

1039
01:06:54.427 --> 01:06:55.511
the goodness.

1040
01:06:55.594 --> 01:06:56.637
It was

1041
01:06:57.304 --> 01:06:59.223
how people talked about her.

1042
01:07:00.099 --> 01:07:02.810
It was her accomplishments,

1043
01:07:02.893 --> 01:07:05.938
and it was just
this beautiful young woman.

1044
01:07:06.897 --> 01:07:08.274
who was trapped in evil.

1045
01:07:09.442 --> 01:07:11.235
And she had been forgotten.

1046
01:07:13.154 --> 01:07:16.657
I just said, "You know,
this is more than just a crime story."

1047
01:07:18.576 --> 01:07:22.788
I wanted to do everything I could
to try to find Sharon's identity.

1048
01:07:22.872 --> 01:07:26.167
I thought that was really important
and I felt, "You know what?"

1049
01:07:27.293 --> 01:07:28.377
"Let's do this book."

1050
01:07:34.675 --> 01:07:39.138
And the only person that knew
her real identity was Franklin Floyd.

1051
01:07:41.057 --> 01:07:43.684
I said, "Let me take a shot

1052
01:07:44.226 --> 01:07:47.438
and see if I can go
interview Franklin Floyd."

1053
01:07:51.901 --> 01:07:53.444
[gate buzzing]

1054
01:07:56.447 --> 01:07:59.575
And I go down there
and they bring me into this county prison.

1055
01:08:00.076 --> 01:08:02.787
[gate buzzes and opens]

1056
01:08:03.454 --> 01:08:06.540
So they brought Floyd
into an interview room to meet with me.

1057
01:08:06.624 --> 01:08:09.627
And they had brought
all of his files with him, too.

1058
01:08:10.669 --> 01:08:11.921
[chains jangling]

1059
01:08:12.004 --> 01:08:14.006
[suspenseful music playing]

1060
01:08:16.133 --> 01:08:19.011
And there were a couple of deputies
standing next to him.

1061
01:08:20.346 --> 01:08:21.472
And then they left.

1062
01:08:22.765 --> 01:08:23.765
[door closes]

1063
01:08:25.101 --> 01:08:26.811
And it's just me and him now in the room.

1064
01:08:29.230 --> 01:08:30.606
And we start talking.

1065
01:08:30.689 --> 01:08:34.443
Actually, I should rephrase that.
He started talking and he didn't stop.

1066
01:08:34.985 --> 01:08:37.863
He thought maybe that
somehow I could help him.

1067
01:08:37.947 --> 01:08:39.707
I could do something
his lawyers couldn't do.

1068
01:08:39.740 --> 01:08:41.951
Tell his story
and somehow that would free him.

1069
01:08:42.868 --> 01:08:45.454
[Floyd]<i> As you go, you're gonna
learn a lot about me.</i>

1070
01:08:45.538 --> 01:08:47.164
<i>I don't care what you write.</i>

1071
01:08:47.248 --> 01:08:50.292
<i>I'll help you tell the truth.</i>

1072
01:08:51.418 --> 01:08:53.587
<i>This is the actual
where I went in the home,</i>

1073
01:08:53.671 --> 01:08:55.172
<i>where my mother abandoned me.</i>

1074
01:08:55.673 --> 01:08:59.009
[Matt] So Franklin Floyd was born in 1943.

1075
01:08:59.885 --> 01:09:01.971
His father died.
He had brothers and sisters.

1076
01:09:02.054 --> 01:09:06.267
Mother couldn't take care of him, sent him
to the Georgia Children's Baptist Home.

1077
01:09:07.017 --> 01:09:09.645
And, you know,
he had a troubled life there.

1078
01:09:09.728 --> 01:09:11.230
[Floyd]<i> The most torturous place...</i>

1079
01:09:11.772 --> 01:09:13.941
<i>Like that old lady, she'd scald my hands.</i>

1080
01:09:14.024 --> 01:09:15.985
<i>And then she pushed my head in the closet.</i>

1081
01:09:16.610 --> 01:09:19.530
<i>They was beating my feet. I couldn't walk.
They swelled up.</i>

1082
01:09:20.281 --> 01:09:23.617
I did see how he was created.

1083
01:09:23.701 --> 01:09:25.369
I did see how the mold was made.

1084
01:09:26.370 --> 01:09:29.248
[Floyd] <i>Boys raped me, beat me,</i>

1085
01:09:29.331 --> 01:09:31.625
<i>made me be their slave and all that.</i>

1086
01:09:32.418 --> 01:09:33.711
<i>When they bathed me</i>

1087
01:09:34.461 --> 01:09:35.462
<i>with certain boys,</i>

1088
01:09:35.546 --> 01:09:37.798
<i>they'd take two fingers and shove it up.</i>

1089
01:09:37.882 --> 01:09:40.134
<i>And they'd get away with it
because I'm small.</i>

1090
01:09:41.886 --> 01:09:45.472
By the time he was 18,
he had real... he had mental issues.

1091
01:09:46.348 --> 01:09:49.351
[Floyd]<i> When I ran away, I joined
the army, drifted around the country,</i>

1092
01:09:50.060 --> 01:09:53.564
<i>and had to steal everywhere I went.</i>

1093
01:09:53.647 --> 01:09:56.483
<i>And then I got accused of a crime,
and then went to prison,</i>

1094
01:09:56.567 --> 01:09:57.651
<i>was abused</i>

1095
01:09:58.194 --> 01:10:01.530
<i>I sure am convicted
of molestation, rape, kidnap.</i>

1096
01:10:01.614 --> 01:10:04.450
<i>And they had no proof of that.
You know that, don't you?</i>

1097
01:10:04.533 --> 01:10:06.827
Any time there was an actual
specific crime, he'd deny it.

1098
01:10:06.911 --> 01:10:10.706
[Floyd] <i>They don't have no proof,
witness or something that says...</i>

1099
01:10:10.789 --> 01:10:13.334
<i>they saw me taking pictures
of somebody with spread legs.</i>

1100
01:10:13.417 --> 01:10:15.169
<i>Don't you get what I'm saying?</i>

1101
01:10:15.252 --> 01:10:18.547
I would ask him about Sharon
and he didn't wanna touch that.

1102
01:10:18.631 --> 01:10:20.901
I'd ask him about Michael,
and he didn't wanna touch that.

1103
01:10:20.925 --> 01:10:22.968
He didn't want to admit to anything.

1104
01:10:24.595 --> 01:10:26.435
I said to him,
"Where did you get Sharon from?"

1105
01:10:26.513 --> 01:10:29.308
He goes, "I didn't get her anywhere.
She just came with me."

1106
01:10:29.391 --> 01:10:30.309
[Floyd]<i> Listen...</i>

1107
01:10:30.392 --> 01:10:31.769
<i>She was a darling.</i>

1108
01:10:32.811 --> 01:10:35.481
<i>And was so smart, and...</i>

1109
01:10:36.148 --> 01:10:39.443
<i>Listen, she loved me no matter what.</i>

1110
01:10:42.863 --> 01:10:46.700
[Matt] He just... He denied everything.
He denied killing Sharon.

1111
01:10:47.618 --> 01:10:50.496
Kidnapping her. He denied killing Michael.

1112
01:10:50.579 --> 01:10:52.873
And he denied killing Cheryl Commesso.

1113
01:10:57.294 --> 01:11:01.548
I didn't learn anything from Floyd
other than he was just clearly psychotic.

1114
01:11:04.468 --> 01:11:08.097
You know, as an investigative journalist,
you try to get down to the truth.

1115
01:11:09.515 --> 01:11:10.975
It was really frustrating,

1116
01:11:11.475 --> 01:11:14.770
by the end of the book, not to...
not to have found out who she was.

1117
01:11:16.522 --> 01:11:18.315
At that point in time,

1118
01:11:18.399 --> 01:11:20.317
you know, we just... the book was done.

1119
01:11:20.859 --> 01:11:22.653
And published.

1120
01:11:22.736 --> 01:11:24.697
[rock music playing]

1121
01:11:27.866 --> 01:11:31.578
Matt Birkbeck interviewed the man
now known as Franklin Floyd in prison.

1122
01:11:31.662 --> 01:11:33.582
Floyd not only kidnapped Sharon
as a little girl,

1123
01:11:33.664 --> 01:11:35.416
he's serving time on death row.

1124
01:11:35.499 --> 01:11:38.460
[newsreader] Matt Birkbeck wrote the book
<i>A Beautiful Child,</i>

1125
01:11:38.544 --> 01:11:40.587
which recounts how, against all odds,

1126
01:11:40.671 --> 01:11:43.340
the girl known as Sharon
blossomed in school.

1127
01:11:43.424 --> 01:11:46.135
[dial-up internet connecting]

1128
01:11:49.763 --> 01:11:51.307
[mouse clicking]

1129
01:11:51.390 --> 01:11:52.766
[computer chimes]

1130
01:11:52.850 --> 01:11:54.435
[Matt] When the book came out,

1131
01:11:54.518 --> 01:11:58.731
it captured the attention
of a couple of websites,

1132
01:11:59.231 --> 01:12:01.150
the Doe Network and Websleuths.

1133
01:12:01.233 --> 01:12:03.277
These are like amateur detectives.

1134
01:12:03.360 --> 01:12:05.904
And then you saw this organic growth.

1135
01:12:05.988 --> 01:12:08.341
You could see different threads.
They were talking about it.

1136
01:12:08.365 --> 01:12:11.245
Who is Sharon Marshall? Could she
be this girl that went missing in Utah?

1137
01:12:11.327 --> 01:12:14.079
Could she be this girl
that went missing in Toronto?

1138
01:12:14.163 --> 01:12:16.203
And it just kept building
and building and building.

1139
01:12:16.248 --> 01:12:17.249
[chiming]

1140
01:12:17.333 --> 01:12:19.543
Over the months, I got more emails.

1141
01:12:19.626 --> 01:12:23.005
People in the US,
people in Canada, people overseas.

1142
01:12:23.088 --> 01:12:25.132
Within six months to a year,

1143
01:12:25.215 --> 01:12:29.011
we had people around the world
trying to find, who is this girl.

1144
01:12:30.346 --> 01:12:33.432
A lot of people were frustrated.
It was like, "Matt, come on!"

1145
01:12:33.515 --> 01:12:36.393
"You know, I'm reading this
and was like, we thought you got it,"

1146
01:12:36.477 --> 01:12:38.270
And I didn't get it.

1147
01:12:38.354 --> 01:12:41.732
And I just... You know, I would answer.
I would answer all these emails.

1148
01:12:41.815 --> 01:12:44.777
I would just say,
"Hey, you know, I did this with the hope

1149
01:12:44.860 --> 01:12:47.905
that we're gonna... you know,
we could find her identity."

1150
01:12:51.158 --> 01:12:54.411
We got a couple of
really good leads actually out of it,

1151
01:12:54.953 --> 01:12:56.793
but we really didn't have any way
to test them.

1152
01:12:56.830 --> 01:12:59.917
But then in 2005,
almost a year after the book came out,

1153
01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:01.126
we got a break.

1154
01:13:01.210 --> 01:13:02.920
I got an anonymous email.

1155
01:13:04.004 --> 01:13:05.464
And it said,

1156
01:13:05.547 --> 01:13:08.967
Would the DNA of
Sharon's daughter help you?

1157
01:13:10.386 --> 01:13:12.388
[hopeful music playing]

1158
01:13:13.347 --> 01:13:14.848
[Megan] I am Megan,

1159
01:13:15.641 --> 01:13:18.102
and I am Sharon's birth daughter.

1160
01:13:19.395 --> 01:13:21.897
I always knew that I was adopted,

1161
01:13:21.980 --> 01:13:26.527
but never felt weird
until I've discovered Matt's book.

1162
01:13:26.610 --> 01:13:30.030
Then it was a lot more
than just being adopted.

1163
01:13:31.782 --> 01:13:33.575
The more I learned,

1164
01:13:33.659 --> 01:13:37.538
the angrier and sadder
I got about everything.

1165
01:13:38.080 --> 01:13:42.251
I mean, that's kind of... kind of been
a progression of emotions since then.

1166
01:13:42.334 --> 01:13:45.796
Everything of this...
since learning about it and...

1167
01:13:45.879 --> 01:13:48.632
has been more anger and more sadness,

1168
01:13:49.550 --> 01:13:52.386
and confusion of how I'm supposed to feel.

1169
01:13:52.469 --> 01:13:55.556
I don't know what my feelings are.
I know I'm mad... [laughs]

1170
01:13:55.639 --> 01:13:58.725
...but I don't know
at what specifically, or why.

1171
01:13:58.809 --> 01:14:02.062
Like, I'm still trying to figure...
figure it all out and process it.

1172
01:14:02.146 --> 01:14:03.564
[somber music playing]

1173
01:14:04.690 --> 01:14:07.985
I learned a lot that I don't like
to think about... about her life.

1174
01:14:11.280 --> 01:14:13.991
No girl should have to go through that.

1175
01:14:15.242 --> 01:14:18.203
From a stranger, much less somebody
that's supposed to be your father.

1176
01:14:18.287 --> 01:14:21.165
Or father figure
or whatever the hell he was. Um...

1177
01:14:22.124 --> 01:14:24.751
Yeah. That's... That's the stuff
I don't like to think about.

1178
01:14:29.840 --> 01:14:35.596
I was a junior in high school
when my aunt discovered Matt's book

1179
01:14:36.346 --> 01:14:37.764
and told my mom about it.

1180
01:14:37.848 --> 01:14:41.727
Um, I remember we were driving home
from The Snowball Stand,

1181
01:14:42.352 --> 01:14:45.314
when my mom told me
that there was more to the story

1182
01:14:45.397 --> 01:14:47.858
than just my birth mother
was killed in a car accident.

1183
01:14:47.941 --> 01:14:49.443
[film whirring]

1184
01:14:49.526 --> 01:14:51.195
[birds chirping]

1185
01:14:52.029 --> 01:14:54.406
[woman] A couple had walked
into an attorney's office

1186
01:14:54.490 --> 01:14:56.700
and they said they couldn't afford
another child.

1187
01:14:56.783 --> 01:14:58.619
"Can you find it someone to adopt?"

1188
01:14:58.702 --> 01:15:02.706
and we walked in and we saw
Clarence and Tonya sitting at the table.

1189
01:15:05.292 --> 01:15:08.545
He just wanted this over with.
He wanted it done. He wanted money.

1190
01:15:09.254 --> 01:15:11.840
He controlled
the whole conversation with her.

1191
01:15:12.674 --> 01:15:14.384
So yeah, I was a little leery.

1192
01:15:14.468 --> 01:15:17.304
But I just feel like God kept telling me,
"This is it."

1193
01:15:17.387 --> 01:15:19.556
[uneasy music playing]

1194
01:15:21.141 --> 01:15:22.893
Six weeks later, Megan was born.

1195
01:15:26.230 --> 01:15:27.814
So we got to the hospital,

1196
01:15:28.732 --> 01:15:30.442
and she'd already delivered.

1197
01:15:36.907 --> 01:15:37.908
She was in the bed

1198
01:15:37.991 --> 01:15:40.452
and I went in there privately,
just her and I.

1199
01:15:43.247 --> 01:15:47.084
And I said, "Did you want to see her?"
She says, "No, I can't."

1200
01:15:48.877 --> 01:15:50.379
And I think back on this day.

1201
01:15:50.462 --> 01:15:52.839
Like why couldn't she
have told me more that day?

1202
01:15:52.923 --> 01:15:55.133
Why couldn't she have said, "I need help."

1203
01:15:55.217 --> 01:15:58.470
Why, when we were alone,
we had the opportunity,

1204
01:15:58.554 --> 01:16:00.013
did you not say,

1205
01:16:01.473 --> 01:16:02.473
"Help me."

1206
01:16:02.975 --> 01:16:06.770
Nobody knows about that. Because it was
just her and I in that room.

1207
01:16:06.853 --> 01:16:10.148
Because the minute Floyd came in,
everything stopped.

1208
01:16:10.232 --> 01:16:11.942
The whole conversation stopped.

1209
01:16:17.823 --> 01:16:19.074
I used to, um...

1210
01:16:19.700 --> 01:16:21.326
I sometimes still do.

1211
01:16:21.410 --> 01:16:25.372
I'll pull up pictures
on the internet of me as a baby,

1212
01:16:25.455 --> 01:16:29.042
and pictures of Michael and
pictures of Sharon and compare them all.

1213
01:16:29.126 --> 01:16:33.839
And just see, um, the cheeks
and the nose for sure came from her.

1214
01:16:33.922 --> 01:16:36.008
And my natural hair color
is the same as hers.

1215
01:16:36.091 --> 01:16:38.802
So, there was... yeah.
I definitely see myself in her.

1216
01:16:38.885 --> 01:16:41.096
[cheerful music playing]

1217
01:16:44.558 --> 01:16:47.144
Growing up you want
to know who you look like.

1218
01:16:47.227 --> 01:16:49.229
What you're supposed to look like. Um...

1219
01:16:50.647 --> 01:16:51.690
Family history.

1220
01:16:51.773 --> 01:16:55.611
And then you go
into your teenage years as a girl.

1221
01:16:55.694 --> 01:16:58.572
Um, I just want to know where I came from.

1222
01:17:02.284 --> 01:17:07.414
In 2010 or 11, I decided to get my DNA.

1223
01:17:07.497 --> 01:17:08.915
Um, it was

1224
01:17:09.625 --> 01:17:13.086
so we could hopefully
find any other family at the time.

1225
01:17:13.629 --> 01:17:15.881
It was exciting. Um...

1226
01:17:15.964 --> 01:17:18.467
There was a potential of finding people.

1227
01:17:19.885 --> 01:17:22.262
[Matt] Sharon had been
pregnant three times.

1228
01:17:22.346 --> 01:17:24.681
Once in high school,
the baby was supposed to be adopted.

1229
01:17:24.765 --> 01:17:25.766
Then it was Michael,

1230
01:17:25.849 --> 01:17:29.102
and here's this third one who was
given up for adoption in New Orleans.

1231
01:17:29.186 --> 01:17:30.437
And that's Megan.

1232
01:17:31.021 --> 01:17:34.358
Having that DNA
and knowing it was a positive match

1233
01:17:34.441 --> 01:17:38.445
meant that it'd just open up
this entire world of possibility.

1234
01:17:38.528 --> 01:17:42.741
And then that's when the National Center
for Missing and Exploited Children

1235
01:17:42.824 --> 01:17:44.034
came to the picture.

1236
01:17:44.117 --> 01:17:46.119
[pensive music playing]

1237
01:17:53.627 --> 01:17:57.130
In 2011, I inherited
a very small case file

1238
01:17:57.214 --> 01:17:59.466
about this girl named Sharon Marshall.

1239
01:18:00.592 --> 01:18:03.053
And I didn't have a lot to go on.

1240
01:18:04.304 --> 01:18:05.931
You know, after I read the book,

1241
01:18:06.014 --> 01:18:08.558
you know, with my little file again,
I had nowhere to turn to.

1242
01:18:08.642 --> 01:18:10.268
I didn't have a law enforcement agency

1243
01:18:10.352 --> 01:18:13.980
but Joe Fitzpatrick was
clearly a big player in all of this.

1244
01:18:14.064 --> 01:18:17.442
He told me about
how the case was inactive with the FBI,

1245
01:18:17.526 --> 01:18:20.570
and that there was never really
a case open on Sharon Marshall.

1246
01:18:20.654 --> 01:18:23.156
He was just able to work
that investigation

1247
01:18:23.240 --> 01:18:25.742
in conjunction with
the abduction of Michael Hughes.

1248
01:18:25.826 --> 01:18:29.871
When Joe stepped up to the plate
and said that he was going to help me, um,

1249
01:18:29.955 --> 01:18:32.082
you know, I... I was... I was ecstatic.

1250
01:18:34.459 --> 01:18:35.669
[Joe] When I received the call

1251
01:18:35.752 --> 01:18:38.463
from the National Center
for Missing and Exploited Children

1252
01:18:38.547 --> 01:18:42.384
I got excited about the fact that
I could get back into this case.

1253
01:18:45.053 --> 01:18:46.555
This was unfinished business.

1254
01:18:46.638 --> 01:18:50.100
This was something
I had made a great deal of progress on,

1255
01:18:50.183 --> 01:18:54.020
but never had a chance to
tie up the loose ends because I retired.

1256
01:18:56.398 --> 01:18:58.608
It gave me just a little hope.

1257
01:19:07.492 --> 01:19:10.620
But we needed... we needed
another shot with Franklin Floyd.

1258
01:19:10.704 --> 01:19:13.290
He was sitting on death row.
He clearly had all the answers.

1259
01:19:13.373 --> 01:19:16.042
So we needed... we needed
another interview with him.

1260
01:19:19.921 --> 01:19:22.716
[man] I got a call from
the National Center for Missing Children,

1261
01:19:22.799 --> 01:19:24.760
from an Ashley Rodriguez.

1262
01:19:24.843 --> 01:19:29.723
I started digging it on the file
and really trying to study who Floyd is.

1263
01:19:29.806 --> 01:19:33.977
He's... He's my target and
I want to know everything I can about him.

1264
01:19:34.060 --> 01:19:35.395
[both sighing]

1265
01:19:37.355 --> 01:19:40.400
I told him, "He's gonna lie to you.
He's gonna lie to you something awful."

1266
01:19:41.026 --> 01:19:43.487
"If you get a truth out of him,
you're gonna be lucky."

1267
01:19:44.070 --> 01:19:45.614
I was not optimistic at all.

1268
01:19:46.448 --> 01:19:48.909
To be honest,
it was kind of like our last resort.

1269
01:19:50.952 --> 01:19:54.664
So the FBI deployed to Florida
to interview Franklin Floyd.

1270
01:19:57.876 --> 01:20:00.003
[man] I had three questions
I wanted answered.

1271
01:20:00.086 --> 01:20:02.172
One was, "Who is Sharon Marshall?"

1272
01:20:03.048 --> 01:20:04.758
"What happened to Michael?"

1273
01:20:04.841 --> 01:20:08.053
And, "Were you responsible
for the death of Sharon?"

1274
01:20:09.137 --> 01:20:11.932
Then I zeroed in
on the first one of who was she.

1275
01:20:12.015 --> 01:20:13.850
Because that's an easy question to answer.

1276
01:20:13.934 --> 01:20:17.312
He may not want to answer,
but it's... he's not admitting to a murder.

1277
01:20:18.647 --> 01:20:22.025
And he would not talk about it.

1278
01:20:27.739 --> 01:20:30.700
He... He just started shutting down,
and he started ranting.

1279
01:20:31.368 --> 01:20:34.368
We didn't even introduce ourselves
as FBI agents before he starts on a rant.

1280
01:20:34.412 --> 01:20:35.914
He thought we were his attorneys.

1281
01:20:35.997 --> 01:20:37.082
We had him seated.

1282
01:20:37.165 --> 01:20:40.877
We were standing while he was doing
this rant for good 45 minutes.

1283
01:20:40.961 --> 01:20:43.338
And I finally said,
"We're not your attorneys."

1284
01:20:44.089 --> 01:20:46.216
And he says, "Well, who the fuck are you?"

1285
01:20:46.842 --> 01:20:48.552
And I said, "We are FBI agents."

1286
01:20:49.427 --> 01:20:52.806
And he... he cocks his head back
and goes, "What do you want?"

1287
01:20:52.889 --> 01:20:56.142
"Well, I'm reopening
the Michael Hughes investigation."

1288
01:20:56.226 --> 01:20:58.478
He goes,
"I'd appreciate it if you'd close it."

1289
01:21:00.230 --> 01:21:01.750
I said, "Well, I'm not gonna do that."

1290
01:21:01.815 --> 01:21:04.609
I said, "You wanted him to be
your... your new Sharon."

1291
01:21:05.193 --> 01:21:07.362
"Sharon's out of the picture,
this is your new Sharon.

1292
01:21:07.445 --> 01:21:09.906
Michael's... Michael's the one
that's gonna replace her."

1293
01:21:09.990 --> 01:21:12.951
And I kept talking to him,
and then he starts crying.

1294
01:21:13.034 --> 01:21:16.788
He was emotional
and that's... that's an opportunity to me.

1295
01:21:16.872 --> 01:21:20.876
And Scott kind of slapped the table
enough to get his attention.

1296
01:21:20.959 --> 01:21:24.588
"How did you kill him, Floyd?"
And his... his crocodile tears are flowing.

1297
01:21:24.671 --> 01:21:27.299
And I raise my voice,
"How did you kill him?"

1298
01:21:27.841 --> 01:21:29.843
He looks at me and says,
"Don't you do that."

1299
01:21:29.926 --> 01:21:32.846
And I finally
hit my fist down on the table,

1300
01:21:33.597 --> 01:21:35.432
"How did you kill him, Floyd?"

1301
01:21:35.515 --> 01:21:37.183
Waterworks turn off.

1302
01:21:37.267 --> 01:21:40.687
"I shot him twice in the back of the head
to make it real quick."

1303
01:21:41.563 --> 01:21:43.565
[tense music playing]

1304
01:21:45.275 --> 01:21:47.986
None of your damn business where he's at.

1305
01:21:48.069 --> 01:21:49.529
[reporter] For more than 20 years

1306
01:21:49.613 --> 01:21:52.240
no one knew what happened
to the little boy,

1307
01:21:52.324 --> 01:21:55.160
but now the FBI believes
they have answers.

1308
01:21:57.329 --> 01:22:01.207
<i>Tears and sadness
from a family who abruptly lost a child.</i>

1309
01:22:01.291 --> 01:22:05.253
And, Father, please tell him hi,
give him a hug, and then a kiss.

1310
01:22:05.754 --> 01:22:07.672
And we'll see him one day.

1311
01:22:10.425 --> 01:22:11.425
It hurts

1312
01:22:11.927 --> 01:22:14.012
to, uh, lose a child.

1313
01:22:15.013 --> 01:22:17.515
- He was almost our child.
- [Merle] Mm-hmm.

1314
01:22:17.599 --> 01:22:21.102
Uh, the adoption papers
were almost completed.

1315
01:22:21.186 --> 01:22:24.856
Uh, and he was kidnapped
before we could complete them.

1316
01:22:24.940 --> 01:22:28.193
All the kids counted him as a brother.

1317
01:22:28.276 --> 01:22:31.988
Uh, so everybody counted him
as one of ours.

1318
01:22:33.198 --> 01:22:34.198
Uh...

1319
01:22:35.158 --> 01:22:36.158
Mmm.

1320
01:22:42.749 --> 01:22:46.252
The FBI says the suspect
in a cold case more than 20 years old

1321
01:22:46.336 --> 01:22:47.879
has confessed to murder.

1322
01:22:47.963 --> 01:22:51.591
Floyd says he buried the boy
near the Oklahoma Texas border.

1323
01:22:52.550 --> 01:22:54.260
We stayed out there for two full days.

1324
01:22:55.095 --> 01:22:57.806
Digging for two days,
sifting for two days.

1325
01:22:57.889 --> 01:22:59.766
And, uh, not a thing.

1326
01:23:01.643 --> 01:23:04.813
You know, we... we gave it a 110 percent.

1327
01:23:05.563 --> 01:23:07.148
And just didn't find anything.

1328
01:23:11.653 --> 01:23:14.781
But I still wanted to know
who Sharon Marshall was.

1329
01:23:15.365 --> 01:23:17.325
And he bought in.

1330
01:23:17.409 --> 01:23:20.412
Partly because Floyd
loved to talk about himself.

1331
01:23:20.495 --> 01:23:23.289
It was funny. He was jumping,
he was telling a lot of stories.

1332
01:23:23.373 --> 01:23:27.585
And then all of a sudden,
he starts talking about how, um...

1333
01:23:28.294 --> 01:23:31.923
How good looking he was,
and he's wearing a bus driver outfit

1334
01:23:32.007 --> 01:23:35.176
in... in Cherryville, North Carolina, and...

1335
01:23:35.927 --> 01:23:38.680
You know, he was the best bus driver
in the world.

1336
01:23:39.305 --> 01:23:44.019
And he tells us
that he meets a girl, Sandy.

1337
01:23:44.102 --> 01:23:46.855
She had just lost
her three kids to the state.

1338
01:23:46.938 --> 01:23:51.693
And Scott asked probably
one of the most brilliant questions.

1339
01:23:51.776 --> 01:23:54.112
He says, "What was your name at the time?"

1340
01:23:55.113 --> 01:23:58.366
Uh, Brandon Cleo Williams
was the name he gave us.

1341
01:23:58.908 --> 01:24:00.910
[suspenseful music playing]

1342
01:24:03.580 --> 01:24:06.416
And that was something
we had never heard before.

1343
01:24:06.499 --> 01:24:10.253
And when... when he gave that name,
it gave us something.

1344
01:24:10.336 --> 01:24:13.548
And not only did he give us that name,
he walked us even further

1345
01:24:13.631 --> 01:24:16.843
and gives us the... the person that he met,

1346
01:24:16.926 --> 01:24:18.386
how they got married.

1347
01:24:19.345 --> 01:24:20.764
He gave us the date.

1348
01:24:20.847 --> 01:24:23.516
He was able to give us
the daughters' names

1349
01:24:23.600 --> 01:24:25.435
and even where the daughters were born.

1350
01:24:25.518 --> 01:24:26.936
So I said, "Who's the oldest?"

1351
01:24:27.020 --> 01:24:29.856
He goes, "Well, that's the one
you're here asking about."

1352
01:24:32.192 --> 01:24:34.652
"Where was she born?" "Livonia, Michigan."

1353
01:24:34.736 --> 01:24:37.781
"How do you know this?"
"I've seen the birth certificate."

1354
01:24:37.864 --> 01:24:41.493
He goes, "That's the girl you're looking.
That's the girl you're here asking about."

1355
01:24:42.744 --> 01:24:44.162
I... I asked him,

1356
01:24:44.245 --> 01:24:46.247
"What... What was the oldest girl's name?"

1357
01:24:47.082 --> 01:24:48.750
And he, "Well, it was Suzanne Sevakis."

1358
01:24:51.086 --> 01:24:52.879
[nostalgic music playing]

1359
01:24:58.301 --> 01:24:59.301
[baby cooing]

1360
01:25:02.680 --> 01:25:04.432
[baby laughing]

1361
01:25:13.775 --> 01:25:15.151
[music fades]

1362
01:25:15.235 --> 01:25:21.533
They told me what her identity was,
I sat there and it was just sort of, uh...

1363
01:25:23.701 --> 01:25:25.787
Oh, I wasn't in a trance. I was just...

1364
01:25:26.663 --> 01:25:29.833
just so delighted.

1365
01:25:29.916 --> 01:25:32.335
You know, I almost cried... [laughs]

1366
01:25:32.418 --> 01:25:34.420
...when I told that to him.

1367
01:25:36.548 --> 01:25:37.715
Oh shoot!

1368
01:25:39.300 --> 01:25:41.010
He goes, "We know her identity."

1369
01:25:41.094 --> 01:25:44.305
And he tells me
her name's Suzanne Sevakis.

1370
01:25:46.516 --> 01:25:47.517
I was like,

1371
01:25:48.852 --> 01:25:50.019
"Holy shit!"

1372
01:25:52.272 --> 01:25:55.233
I don't think relief is the right word
but that's kind of what I felt.

1373
01:25:55.316 --> 01:25:58.736
It was just like, it's over.
Like we now know who she is.

1374
01:26:02.365 --> 01:26:05.326
[Scott] The next day,
we get the birth certificate back.

1375
01:26:05.827 --> 01:26:08.413
And that birth certificate has
her parents' names on it.

1376
01:26:08.496 --> 01:26:10.957
Sandra Brandenburg and Clifford Sevakis.

1377
01:26:11.875 --> 01:26:14.252
Oh, by the way, they're both still alive.

1378
01:26:15.086 --> 01:26:17.088
[suspenseful music playing]

1379
01:26:25.680 --> 01:26:27.807
[Sandra] The FBI showed up on the door.

1380
01:26:28.808 --> 01:26:32.103
And then they showed me Susie's picture,
and I said, "That's my daughter."

1381
01:26:32.187 --> 01:26:33.897
"Do you know where she is?"

1382
01:26:36.482 --> 01:26:38.484
[gentle music playing]

1383
01:26:39.235 --> 01:26:40.737
She was very smart.

1384
01:26:41.696 --> 01:26:42.947
Very silly.

1385
01:26:44.908 --> 01:26:46.534
And very quick-witted.

1386
01:26:49.329 --> 01:26:52.832
I was 18 when I got pregnant
and I was 19 when she was born.

1387
01:26:55.043 --> 01:26:56.920
I was 17 when I started dating.

1388
01:26:58.087 --> 01:27:00.381
Cliff and I were in high school together.

1389
01:27:01.424 --> 01:27:03.885
[Cliff] She was about
two years younger than me.

1390
01:27:04.719 --> 01:27:07.555
But she was, uh, smart and funny,

1391
01:27:08.348 --> 01:27:09.849
and I was so smitten.

1392
01:27:10.767 --> 01:27:13.228
We were an item
all the way through high school.

1393
01:27:14.771 --> 01:27:17.899
[Sandra] We got married
right at the end of high school.

1394
01:27:19.317 --> 01:27:22.153
I got pregnant
a few months after we got married.

1395
01:27:22.779 --> 01:27:24.197
I was excited.

1396
01:27:25.740 --> 01:27:27.992
I was happy.

1397
01:27:28.785 --> 01:27:31.496
And I... I couldn't wait
for the baby to come.

1398
01:27:33.331 --> 01:27:36.584
He was in Vietnam when she was born.

1399
01:27:37.168 --> 01:27:38.503
It was hard.

1400
01:27:38.586 --> 01:27:41.339
[Cliff] I had an R&R for a week,

1401
01:27:41.422 --> 01:27:43.675
and that's when
I saw Suzanne for the first time.

1402
01:27:43.758 --> 01:27:45.260
She was six months old.

1403
01:27:46.094 --> 01:27:48.346
It was a beautiful little cherub.

1404
01:27:49.555 --> 01:27:50.640
I was proud.

1405
01:27:51.307 --> 01:27:53.768
Your heart grows bigger
when you have a child.

1406
01:27:55.395 --> 01:27:57.522
But, uh, when I went to Vietnam,

1407
01:27:58.064 --> 01:28:01.776
you leave the rest of the world behind
and that's your whole world.

1408
01:28:02.902 --> 01:28:08.366
I was different when I got back
and, uh, she was seeing another guy.

1409
01:28:08.950 --> 01:28:11.911
And that's when Sandy told me
she wanted to divorce.

1410
01:28:13.496 --> 01:28:15.790
[Sandra] I had started seeing another man,

1411
01:28:16.332 --> 01:28:18.626
and I got pregnant with Allison and Amy.

1412
01:28:19.752 --> 01:28:21.337
But we got divorced.

1413
01:28:22.380 --> 01:28:26.718
And I moved the girls and I
to a trailer in a mobile home park.

1414
01:28:28.094 --> 01:28:31.180
The mobile home park was like on a hill.

1415
01:28:31.264 --> 01:28:36.269
You know, the tornado hit out of the blue,
I mean, and tipped my trailer sideways.

1416
01:28:41.607 --> 01:28:46.321
After the tornado, I had,
I guess now they would call it PTSD.

1417
01:28:47.113 --> 01:28:48.614
I can remember,

1418
01:28:50.450 --> 01:28:54.829
at one point, sitting in the corner,
in the living room, on the floor.

1419
01:28:56.331 --> 01:28:58.875
And... And the girls saying,
"Mommy! Mommy! Mommy!"

1420
01:28:58.958 --> 01:29:00.209
and I couldn't move.

1421
01:29:02.670 --> 01:29:06.799
I went to Social Services because
I thought that's what you did to get help.

1422
01:29:07.759 --> 01:29:09.677
They... They took the children.

1423
01:29:09.761 --> 01:29:11.929
I remember telling her and crying,

1424
01:29:12.013 --> 01:29:14.849
"It's not safe.
I can't take care of them."

1425
01:29:14.932 --> 01:29:17.560
The lady in the front
of the Social Services office, she said,

1426
01:29:17.643 --> 01:29:19.771
"Honey, go to church. You'll feel better."

1427
01:29:21.773 --> 01:29:26.402
Department of Social Services
called me up on the phone and said, uh.

1428
01:29:26.486 --> 01:29:29.781
"We want to adopt
all three girls out to one family."

1429
01:29:29.864 --> 01:29:33.034
"They're attached to each other
and we don't want to break up the set."

1430
01:29:34.327 --> 01:29:39.123
They gave me a choice, either adopt
all three or give up all three.

1431
01:29:42.126 --> 01:29:44.170
It was pretty rough on me.

1432
01:29:44.253 --> 01:29:46.172
I spent a weekend

1433
01:29:48.257 --> 01:29:51.511
drinking too much
and thinking about it too much.

1434
01:29:52.053 --> 01:29:55.056
And, uh, at the time,
I was living with my parents,

1435
01:29:55.139 --> 01:29:56.933
I was unemployed.

1436
01:29:57.016 --> 01:30:00.520
I was, uh, 23 years old, I think.

1437
01:30:01.187 --> 01:30:05.441
And I just didn't think I was going to be
a good parent, at that point.

1438
01:30:05.525 --> 01:30:08.945
I was still kind of messed up
from Vietnam.

1439
01:30:10.154 --> 01:30:13.408
[bell tolling]

1440
01:30:14.367 --> 01:30:16.595
[Sandra] When I went to that church,
I know I was crying,

1441
01:30:16.619 --> 01:30:19.497
'cause I was crying all the time,
and I couldn't stop crying.

1442
01:30:19.997 --> 01:30:21.332
And that's where I met him.

1443
01:30:23.209 --> 01:30:25.294
He just came and sat down,

1444
01:30:25.378 --> 01:30:29.632
and he just started talking to me
in... in a calm voice.

1445
01:30:30.133 --> 01:30:31.551
You know, "What's wrong?"

1446
01:30:32.135 --> 01:30:34.095
"God sent me here to help you."

1447
01:30:35.012 --> 01:30:37.265
He said, "We'll go get your children."

1448
01:30:38.599 --> 01:30:41.727
"We'll get married, and I'll take care
of you and the children,

1449
01:30:41.811 --> 01:30:43.604
and everything will be all right."

1450
01:30:45.606 --> 01:30:49.569
After we were together,
he would do things that were scary things.

1451
01:30:52.155 --> 01:30:56.075
Once I realized the situation I was in
with him, I didn't know what to do.

1452
01:30:57.577 --> 01:31:01.080
And he... he had a knife
that he carried all the time.

1453
01:31:01.664 --> 01:31:04.959
and he would reach down
to his side where the knife was,

1454
01:31:05.042 --> 01:31:07.712
and he'd say, "Do you think
you're going to leave me?"

1455
01:31:09.088 --> 01:31:10.339
That's not happening.

1456
01:31:15.052 --> 01:31:18.639
One time I needed
to buy the girls' diapers.

1457
01:31:18.723 --> 01:31:21.184
I had written a bad check at 7-Eleven.

1458
01:31:21.934 --> 01:31:23.895
So I got 30 days in jail.

1459
01:31:27.732 --> 01:31:29.859
And that's when he took my children.

1460
01:31:31.777 --> 01:31:34.322
I went to the police station immediately

1461
01:31:34.864 --> 01:31:37.450
and told the police
he had taken my children.

1462
01:31:38.326 --> 01:31:40.786
The police said,
"Are you legally married to him?"

1463
01:31:40.870 --> 01:31:41.870
And I said, "Yes."

1464
01:31:41.913 --> 01:31:45.917
And the police said, "That's a civil thing
you'll have to take care of yourself."

1465
01:31:47.585 --> 01:31:50.338
And I just kept getting louder
and louder and louder,

1466
01:31:50.421 --> 01:31:52.757
and they escorted me
out of the police station.

1467
01:31:55.676 --> 01:31:57.678
At some point,
and I don't know when exactly,

1468
01:31:57.762 --> 01:32:01.766
he had taken Allison and Amy
and dropped them off at the orphanage,

1469
01:32:01.849 --> 01:32:03.392
and took Susie and left.

1470
01:32:03.476 --> 01:32:05.478
[disturbing music playing]

1471
01:32:09.065 --> 01:32:10.942
You know, you can't go back and say,

1472
01:32:11.526 --> 01:32:12.568
"If I didn't..."

1473
01:32:13.069 --> 01:32:14.070
[sniffling]

1474
01:32:15.279 --> 01:32:19.534
"If I had found some way to get help."

1475
01:32:20.451 --> 01:32:23.829
"To get away from the whole situation,
then it never would've happened."

1476
01:32:25.331 --> 01:32:28.918
And I was supposed to be her mother
and protect her from that monster.

1477
01:32:29.752 --> 01:32:30.752
And I didn't.

1478
01:32:33.256 --> 01:32:35.967
I'm actually very angry at Sharon's mom.

1479
01:32:36.842 --> 01:32:39.387
I don't believe for one second that,

1480
01:32:39.470 --> 01:32:43.432
because this was back in the day,
that she couldn't find her child.

1481
01:32:43.516 --> 01:32:46.102
I was taken in 1976.

1482
01:32:46.644 --> 01:32:51.649
And for almost five years,
my mom contacted everyone.

1483
01:32:52.149 --> 01:32:53.234
Her Senator,

1484
01:32:53.859 --> 01:32:55.903
the Mayor, she went on TV.

1485
01:32:56.445 --> 01:32:58.990
She did everything she could.

1486
01:33:00.116 --> 01:33:02.702
And she wasn't an affluent person,

1487
01:33:02.785 --> 01:33:06.539
but she spent
all of the money she could looking for me.

1488
01:33:06.622 --> 01:33:08.874
My mother did everything,

1489
01:33:08.958 --> 01:33:11.127
and I just want to know why.

1490
01:33:12.420 --> 01:33:14.880
Why didn't she try harder?

1491
01:33:16.632 --> 01:33:19.802
I'll be honest.
I did reach out to her grandmother.

1492
01:33:22.221 --> 01:33:23.264
That didn't go well.

1493
01:33:23.889 --> 01:33:26.434
It's... It's that, "I don't care" attitude.

1494
01:33:26.517 --> 01:33:30.271
When you reach out to someone
and they... they have no interest,

1495
01:33:31.272 --> 01:33:32.940
that, to me... mm-mm.

1496
01:33:34.150 --> 01:33:35.150
You don't care?

1497
01:33:35.776 --> 01:33:38.362
You don't want to know?
What kind of person are you?

1498
01:33:38.446 --> 01:33:40.615
I... I just have a problem with that.

1499
01:33:40.698 --> 01:33:42.700
[wind whooshing]

1500
01:33:46.662 --> 01:33:50.291
[Matt] In 2003, when I was in Tulsa,
and I went to visit the cemetery,

1501
01:33:50.374 --> 01:33:53.544
I thought, you know, "Wouldn't it be cool

1502
01:33:53.628 --> 01:33:56.339
to come back here one day
and replace this headstone?"

1503
01:33:56.422 --> 01:33:59.216
It just had one name in it, Tonya.
And that bothered me.

1504
01:34:00.009 --> 01:34:02.845
So after learning her identity,

1505
01:34:02.928 --> 01:34:04.847
we decided, you know, I spoke with Megan.

1506
01:34:04.930 --> 01:34:08.100
And I said,
"Hey, you know, uh, let's do this."

1507
01:34:09.226 --> 01:34:14.607
Matt wanted my input on what
should be written on the headstone.

1508
01:34:15.358 --> 01:34:17.860
And I was like, "Holy crap.
That's a lot of responsibility."

1509
01:34:18.778 --> 01:34:22.782
She touched a lot of people in her life,
and I wanted to make sure that

1510
01:34:22.865 --> 01:34:26.077
it showed that she was
everything to everybody.

1511
01:34:27.370 --> 01:34:28.913
[bell tolling]

1512
01:34:31.999 --> 01:34:34.039
[minister] Father, I thank you
for this opportunity.

1513
01:34:34.085 --> 01:34:37.380
And I pray that you'd bring the comfort,
the strength, the heart

1514
01:34:37.463 --> 01:34:38.964
to the lives of those here.

1515
01:34:39.048 --> 01:34:41.759
Not only here today,
but wherever they might be.

1516
01:34:43.928 --> 01:34:45.930
[somber music playing]

1517
01:34:49.475 --> 01:34:50.601
There she is.

1518
01:34:51.977 --> 01:34:53.062
There she is.

1519
01:34:55.147 --> 01:34:58.567
[Matt] She was just 20 years old
when she died in 1990.

1520
01:34:59.860 --> 01:35:04.365
And it wasn't until June 2017
that we could change her tombstone.

1521
01:35:04.448 --> 01:35:07.076
And finally, put her real name there.

1522
01:35:09.620 --> 01:35:13.165
[Megan] She was the definition of a friend
to everyone.

1523
01:35:13.749 --> 01:35:16.711
The sound voice
and the... the support system for people,

1524
01:35:16.794 --> 01:35:21.340
which is absolutely insane
because she had none of that at home.

1525
01:35:21.424 --> 01:35:24.009
And she did it all with such poise.

1526
01:35:24.093 --> 01:35:26.095
[somber music continues]

1527
01:35:31.642 --> 01:35:35.187
[Lynn] She finally had
the memorial service that she deserved.

1528
01:35:36.313 --> 01:35:41.193
That put a semicolon, for me, on there.

1529
01:35:41.777 --> 01:35:43.654
And, finally, she's at rest.

1530
01:35:45.239 --> 01:35:47.116
But she's still alive in my heart.

1531
01:35:49.452 --> 01:35:53.372
And when I go, maybe that's when
the period is. [chuckles]

1532
01:35:55.958 --> 01:35:58.461
[Jenny] It was, um, beautiful.

1533
01:35:58.544 --> 01:36:01.297
It was... It was wonderful
to find out who she was.

1534
01:36:02.131 --> 01:36:04.550
Um, I remember just,

1535
01:36:06.093 --> 01:36:08.053
"Girl, I got your back," you know?

1536
01:36:10.222 --> 01:36:14.143
[Cliff] One of the things that got me most
was that she never knew who she was.

1537
01:36:16.604 --> 01:36:20.941
Knowing the people that were
part of her life really helped me out.

1538
01:36:22.193 --> 01:36:25.112
'Cause they don't have
such positive memories of her.

1539
01:36:25.613 --> 01:36:30.075
You get the feeling that,
at times, she was, uh,

1540
01:36:30.701 --> 01:36:32.578
making the most of the life she had.

1541
01:36:36.582 --> 01:36:39.502
I was excited... excited that...

1542
01:36:39.585 --> 01:36:41.295
[inhales deeply, clears throat]

1543
01:36:41.378 --> 01:36:44.632
...we put her name
on a tombstone and it's her.

1544
01:36:48.135 --> 01:36:51.180
[Joe] It was important
to all of us, you know, it was...

1545
01:36:51.263 --> 01:36:53.766
This was who she really was.
This is really her dad.

1546
01:36:53.849 --> 01:36:55.684
This is their daughter, you know?

1547
01:36:56.477 --> 01:36:58.157
Here's where she is,
here's where she lies,

1548
01:36:58.187 --> 01:36:59.980
and here's what her true name is.

1549
01:37:06.529 --> 01:37:07.947
Sheriff, just thank you.

1550
01:37:09.031 --> 01:37:12.660
I got so many new relationships
and more family than I needed.

1551
01:37:12.743 --> 01:37:14.328
[all laugh]

1552
01:37:14.411 --> 01:37:18.249
And I hope I can be half the mom
that she was or wanted to be.

1553
01:37:19.834 --> 01:37:24.296
Becoming a parent gave me
even more respect for my birth mother

1554
01:37:24.380 --> 01:37:27.633
because she gave up two children,

1555
01:37:27.716 --> 01:37:28.926
if not more,

1556
01:37:29.009 --> 01:37:32.304
knowing that it was better for the kids.

1557
01:37:34.974 --> 01:37:38.185
My son is named Michael.
He's named after my brother.

1558
01:37:38.811 --> 01:37:42.940
Michael didn't get to live out his name
and I wanted that name to keep going.

1559
01:37:45.025 --> 01:37:49.613
What I can do is, I can't talk to Suzanne,
but I can talk to Megan.

1560
01:37:50.155 --> 01:37:52.157
[solemn music playing]

1561
01:37:53.826 --> 01:37:56.996
And that will... that will do.

1562
01:38:01.750 --> 01:38:03.419
[Megan] So I'm trying to figure out me,

1563
01:38:03.502 --> 01:38:07.089
but I know that this story
is going to help somebody.

1564
01:38:07.590 --> 01:38:12.344
I just got to figure out all the pieces
and how it shaped me,

1565
01:38:12.428 --> 01:38:14.597
And then I know
I'm gonna be able to share this.

1566
01:38:19.977 --> 01:38:22.563
[Heather] I just know
that she had a chance.

1567
01:38:23.939 --> 01:38:26.108
She would have been one of those persons

1568
01:38:26.191 --> 01:38:29.904
that would have been able
to overcome what happened to her.

1569
01:38:31.071 --> 01:38:33.741
If she had just gotten away from him,

1570
01:38:34.366 --> 01:38:37.369
she would have been an amazing survivor.

1571
01:38:39.538 --> 01:38:41.540
She had so much potential.

1572
01:38:43.584 --> 01:38:46.045
She had something to offer the world.

1573
01:38:46.837 --> 01:38:49.423
She really had a gift, and...

1574
01:38:52.426 --> 01:38:54.553
that's how I'll always remember her.

1575
01:38:56.138 --> 01:38:58.140
[solemn music continues]

1576
01:39:19.078 --> 01:39:21.080
[gentle music playing]
